# GoGoCash 1.1 — Next.js 15 Rules

## Framework
- App Router ONLY. Never use `pages/` directory.
- Server Components by default. Use `'use client'` only when the component needs interactivity, browser APIs, or React hooks.
- i18n routing via `next-intl`. All pages live under `src/app/[locale]/`. Never create routes outside the locale wrapper.
- Images: always `next/image`, never `<img>`. Set `width`, `height`, or `fill` explicitly.
- Fonts: use `next/font`. Never import font CSS from external URLs.

## TypeScript
- Strict mode is ON. No `any`. No `as unknown as X` casts.
- All component props defined in a co-located `interface.ts` file, exported as `I{ComponentName}Props`.
- All API response types defined in `src/interfaces/`. Import from there, never inline.
- Use `type` for unions/intersections. Use `interface` for object shapes and component props.

## Styling
- **Tailwind CSS ONLY.** No MUI, no Emotion, no styled-components, no inline `style={{}}` except for dynamic values that cannot be expressed in Tailwind.
- Colors: ALWAYS use CSS variables (`var(--primary-1)`, `var(--cashback-green)`, etc.). Never hardcode hex values.
- Spacing follows 4px grid. Use Tailwind spacing scale (`p-1`=4px, `p-2`=8px, etc.).
- Dark mode via `data-theme` attribute on `<html>`. CSS variables override in `[data-theme='dark']`.

## Components
- One component per file. File name = component name in PascalCase.
- Every component folder has: `ComponentName.tsx`, `interface.ts`, `index.ts`.
- Every component must handle: loading state (`<Skeleton />`), empty state (custom UI), error state (message + retry).
- No component renders `null` for empty — always render a meaningful empty state.

## Data Fetching
- Server components: use `fetch()` with `next: { revalidate: 60 }` for static-ish data.
- Client components: use TanStack Query (`@tanstack/react-query`) exclusively. No `useEffect` + `fetch` patterns.
- All API calls go through `src/lib/apiClient.ts` (Axios with auth interceptor).
- Cache times: merchant list = 5min, wallet balance = 30s, categories = 10min.

## State Management
- Global auth state: `src/providers/AuthProvider.tsx` (NextAuth SessionProvider wrapper).
- Global wallet state: `src/providers/WalletProvider.tsx` (Wagmi WagmiProvider).
- Feature state: local `useState` or TanStack Query cache. No Redux.
- Never store server-fetched data in React context — that's TanStack Query's job.

## Routing & Middleware
- `middleware.ts` handles TWO concerns in this order: (1) next-intl locale detection, (2) NextAuth session guard.
- Protected routes: `/(page)/*`, `/wallet`, `/profile`, `/history`, `/notification`, `/affiliate`.
- Public routes: `/auth/*`, `/shop` (browse-only mode).

## Security
- Never log `session`, `token`, or any credential to `console`.
- All user inputs validated with `zod` before API calls.
- `NEXT_PUBLIC_*` vars only for non-sensitive config. Secrets stay server-side.

## Performance
- Dynamic import for any component > 10kb that is not in the critical render path: `dynamic(() => import('./Component'), { ssr: false })`.
- Virtualize lists > 50 items using `react-virtual`.
- Memoize with `useMemo`/`useCallback` ONLY when there is a measurable performance issue. Do not pre-optimize.

## Accessibility
- Semantic HTML: `<button>` for actions, `<a>` for navigation, `<nav>`, `<main>`, `<section>` correctly.
- All interactive elements have `aria-label` if no visible text.
- Keyboard navigable. Focus ring visible.

## Testing
- Jest + React Testing Library.
- One `__tests__/Component.test.tsx` per component in `src/components/common/`.
- Test: renders correctly, handles loading state, handles error state, user interactions fire correct callbacks.
- Mock all API calls. Never call real network in tests.
